title: Prime Minister's Questions
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: commons
view-if: pmqs_timer <= 0
on-arrival: pmqs_timer = 2; month_actions += 1

= Prime Minister's Questions

Tuesday and Thursday, 3.15pm. Callaghan is an old hand at the dispatch box, and he enjoys patronising you.

- @attack: Go for the jugular.
- @careful: A careful, detailed question.
- @easy_discard

@attack
on-arrival: {!
var chance = 45 + (Q.thatcher_rating - Q.callaghan_rating) + 3 * Q.strike_wave;
if (chance < 10) {
    chance = 10;
} else if (chance > 90) {
    chance = 90;
}
Q.pmq_success = (Math.random() * 100 < chance) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: attack_win if pmq_success = 1; attack_lose if pmq_success = 0

@attack_win
on-arrival: thatcher_rating += 3; callaghan_rating -= 2

You land the blow. Callaghan's avuncular manner slips, and the sketch-writers notice.

@attack_lose
on-arrival: thatcher_rating -= 2; callaghan_rating += 1

Callaghan swats the question aside with a joke at your expense. Labour's benches roar.

@careful
on-arrival: thatcher_rating += 1

A precise question on the money supply figures. The Prime Minister bluffs, and the people who matter notice.
